This repository is a hard fork of duckdb/duckdb-java at tag v1.5.3.0. The
upstream MIT LICENSE is preserved verbatim. Modifications introduced by
Haybarn:

  - Java package renamed: org.duckdb -> farm.query.haybarn (and likewise
    org.duckdb.io / org.duckdb.user / test packages). All 80 Java source
    files moved under src/{main,test}/java/farm/query/haybarn/.
  - Driver SPI entry-point class renamed: DuckDBDriver -> HaybarnDriver.
    META-INF/services/java.sql.Driver updated to farm.query.haybarn.HaybarnDriver.
    Other DuckDB* class names are kept (DuckDBConnection, DuckDBAppender,
    DuckDBResultSet, etc.) so user code that casts to them needs only an
    import-source change.
  - JDBC URL prefix: jdbc:duckdb: -> jdbc:haybarn: .
  - Maven coordinates: org.duckdb:duckdb_jdbc -> farm.query.haybarn:haybarn_jdbc.
  - JNI native library: libduckdb_java.so / duckdb_java.{def,exp,map} ->
    libhaybarn_java.so / haybarn_java.{def,exp,map}. JNI function-name prefix
    Java_org_duckdb_ -> Java_farm_query_haybarn_ . The internal Java native
    method names (DuckDBNative.duckdb_jdbc_*) are kept since they're never
    user-visible.
  - Build artifacts: duckdb_jdbc.jar (+ _nolib / _tests / per-classifier)
    -> haybarn_jdbc.jar.
  - OSGi MANIFEST.MF rebranded to Haybarn (Query Farm LLC, hello@query.farm).
  - The vendored src/duckdb/ DuckDB source tree was re-vendored via vendor.py
    from Query-farm-haybarn/haybarn (haybarn branch), so the embedded engine
    carries the Haybarn extension trust root (single Haybarn public key, no
    DuckDB core/community keys) and the Haybarn extension repository URLs
    (https://haybarn-extensions.query.farm/{core,community}).

Source for the underlying DuckDB engine, as modified by Haybarn, is at:
https://github.com/Query-farm-haybarn/haybarn

The original duckdb-java project lives at:
https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb-java
